{title: A Thousand Years in Your Sight}
{subtitle: Psalms 90:4}
{key: Dm}
{tempo: 79}
{time: 3/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Dm] | ×8

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Lord, you have been our dwelling place
Through all generations
Before the mountains were born
From everlasting to everlasting you are God
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
You return mortals to dust
Saying, Return, you children of man
For a thousand years in your sight
Are like a day that has just gone by
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
Like [Bb]grass that springs up [C]in the morn[Dm]ing
In the [Bb]morning it blooms and [C]flourish[Dm]es
By [Bb]evening it with[C]ers and dries up
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
From [Dm]everlasting to everlasting you are God
{end_of_verse}
